<section class="section" id="overview">
 <div class="container">
  <div class="section-head reveal"><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / Product overview</div><h2>Not just screens.<br><em>A service journey.</em></h2></div><p>Good mobile products reduce friction between what a person needs and what they need to do next. MotoServis is structured around the real tasks of motorcycle ownership.</p></div>
  <div class="overview-grid">
   <div class="overview-copy reveal"><h3>Make routine maintenance feel <span class="serif accent">effortless.</span></h3><p>Riders can explore service options, understand what a service includes, find a workshop, choose a suitable appointment and return to their profile or service history later. The interface brings these related tasks into a single, recognizable experience.</p><p>The product concept focuses on clear hierarchy, strong calls to action, predictable steps and visible feedback—so users are not left guessing what happens after a tap.</p></div>
   <div class="stat-grid reveal delay-1">
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">01</div><strong>Discover</strong><p>Explore services, promotions and nearby workshops.</p></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">02</div><strong>Book</strong><p>Choose a service and move through a clear booking flow.</p></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">03</div><strong>Manage</strong><p>Keep profile details and order information accessible.</p></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">04</div><strong>Return</strong><p>Revisit maintenance and service information when needed.</p></div>
   </div>
  </div>
  <div class="capability-strip reveal">
   <div class="capability"><span class="symbol">⌕</span><div><b>Fast discovery</b><small>Services and workshop browsing</small></div></div>
   <div class="capability"><span class="symbol">◷</span><div><b>Structured booking</b><small>Service selection to confirmation</small></div></div>
   <div class="capability"><span class="symbol">▣</span><div><b>Account hub</b><small>Profile and order access</small></div></div>
   <div class="capability"><span class="symbol">↗</span><div><b>Room to scale</b><small>Modular feature and data concepts</small></div></div>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-light" id="experience">
 <div class="container">
  <div class="section-head reveal"><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / The mobile experience</div><h2>Designed for the<br><em>whole rider journey.</em></h2></div><p>From the first glance at the dashboard to the details of a selected service, every part of the experience has a job to do.</p></div>
  <div class="journey-intro reveal">
   <div class="chapter"><span>01</span> THE PRODUCT</div>
   <div><h3>One app. Every step of the journey.</h3><p>Use the visuals below to tell the product story in sequence: the actual mobile interface first, the main user areas next, then the technology and feature overview.</p><div class="journey-tags"><span>Home &amp; discovery</span><span>Service booking</span><span>Workshop details</span><span>Rider profile</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="visual-stack">
   <figure class="visual-card reveal">
    <div class="visual-toolbar"><span><i></i> MOBILE INTERFACE / APP SCREENS</span><span class="count">01 / 04</span></div>
    <div class="visual-image app-image"><img src="/assets/projects/labib/motointerface.png" alt="MotoServis mobile app screen overview" loading="lazy" onerror="this.style.display='none';this.parentElement.nextElementSibling.style.display='block'"></div>
