<section class="section arch-section" id="architecture">
 <div class="container">
  <div class="section-head reveal"><div><div class="eyebrow">03 / Application architecture</div><h2>From interaction<br>to <em>implementation.</em></h2></div><p>A strong app architecture keeps the interface responsive while separating presentation, state, business rules and data access. This conceptual diagram makes those responsibilities visible.</p></div>
  <div class="architecture reveal">
   <div class="architecture-top"><h3>Development architecture</h3><small>TOP-DOWN SYSTEM VIEW · CONCEPTUAL</small></div>
   <div class="arch-tree">
    <div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon">▣</span><div><b>Presentation layer</b><small>Flutter screens · widgets · navigation · forms</small></div><em>01 / UI</em></div>
    <div class="arch-connector"></div>
    <div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon">⌘</span><div><b>State management</b><small>GetX controllers · reactive state · loading and error states</small></div><em>02 / STATE</em></div>
    <div class="arch-connector"></div>
    <div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon">◇</span><div><b>Application &amp; business logic</b><small>Validation · booking rules · service selection · workflow orchestration</small></div><em>03 / LOGIC</em></div>
    <div class="arch-connector"></div>
    <div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon">⇄</span><div><b>Repository / data access</b><small>Data models · API clients · local persistence adapters</small></div><em>04 / DATA</em></div>
    <div class="arch-connector"></div>
    <div class="arch-branch">
     <div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon">↗</span><div><b>REST API</b><small>Remote data integration</small></div><em>NETWORK</em></div>
     <div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon">◈</span><div><b>Firebase</b><small>Authentication / backend services where used</small></div><em>CLOUD</em></div>
     <div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon">▤</span><div><b>SQLite</b><small>Local data persistence</small></div><em>LOCAL</em></div>
    </div>
   </div>
   <p class="arch-note">Architecture is a presentation model based on the technology concepts supplied for this project. Confirm actual package usage, integrations and layer boundaries against the source code before describing them as implemented production components.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="visual-stack" style="margin-top:24px">
   <figure class="visual-card reveal">
    <div class="visual-toolbar"><span><i></i> ORIGINAL ARCHITECTURE VISUAL</span><span class="count">REFERENCE</span></div>
    <div class="visual-image"><img src="/assets/projects/labib/motoarchite.png" class="wide" alt="MotoServis original development architecture diagram" loading="lazy" onerror="this.style.display='none';this.parentElement.nextElementSibling.style.display='block'"></div>
    <div class="visual-placeholder"><strong>Architecture reference image</strong><p>Place motoarchite.png in /assets/projects/labib/ to display the supplied diagram.</p></div>
    <figcaption class="visual-caption"><strong>Architecture reference</strong><p>The original diagram can be inspected horizontally on smaller screens.</p><span class="image-note">SOURCE VISUAL</span></figcaption>
   </figure>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="section data-section" id="data-model">
 <div class="container">
  <div class="section-head reveal"><div><div class="eyebrow">04 / Data model &amp; ER diagram</div><h2>Every journey leaves<br><em>a clear record.</em></h2></div><p>The data model explains how users, motorcycles, workshops, service definitions, bookings and orders can relate. The diagram is illustrative—not a claim that these exact tables exist in a production database.</p></div>
  <div class="erd-wrap reveal">
   <div class="erd-canvas">
    <svg class="erd-lines" viewBox="0 0 1000 610" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-label="Entity relationship connectors">
     <g fill="none" stroke="#e12a36" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-dasharray="5 4" opacity=".8">
      <path d="M500 125 V155 H100 V205"/><path d="M500 125 V205"/><path d="M500 125 V155 H900 V205"/>
      <path d="M100 330 V380 H300 V440"/><path d="M500 330 V385 H300 V440"/><path d="M500 330 V385 H700 V440"/><path d="M900 330 V380 H700 V440"/>
     </g>
     <g fill="#e12a36"><circle cx="100" cy="205" r="3"/><circle cx="500" cy="205" r="3"/><circle cx="900" cy="205" r="3"/><circle cx="300" cy="440" r="3"/><circle cx="700" cy="440" r="3"/></g>
    </svg>
    <div class="erd-grid">
     <div class="entity e-users"><div class="entity-head">USERS <span>PK</span></div><div class="entity-fields"><div><b>PK</b> user_id</div><div>full_name</div><div>email</div><div>phone</div><div>created_at</div></div></div>
     <div class="entity e-bike"><div class="entity-head">MOTORCYCLES <span>PK</span></div><div class="entity-fields"><div><b>PK</b> motorcycle_id</div><div><b>FK</b> user_id</div><div>make / model</div><div>registration_no</div></div></div>
     <div class="entity e-workshop"><div class="entity-head">WORKSHOPS <span>PK</span></div><div class="entity-fields"><div><b>PK</b> workshop_id</div><div>name</div><div>address</div><div>contact_phone</div><div>availability</div></div></div>
     <div class="entity e-service"><div class="entity-head">SERVICES <span>PK</span></div><div class="entity-fields"><div><b>PK</b> service_id</div><div>service_name</div><div>description</div><div>base_price</div><div>duration_mins</div></div></div>
     <div class="entity e-booking"><div class="entity-head">BOOKINGS <span>PK</span></div><div class="entity-fields"><div><b>PK</b> booking_id</div><div><b>FK</b> user_id</div><div><b>FK</b> workshop_id</div><div><b>FK</b> service_id</div><div>slot / status</div></div></div>
     <div class="entity e-order"><div class="entity-head">ORDERS &amp; PARTS <span>PK</span></div><div class="entity-fields"><div><b>PK</b> order_id</div><div><b>FK</b> user_id</div><div>order_status</div><div>total_amount</div><div>created_at</div></div></div>
    </div>
   </div>
  </div>
  <div class="erd-legend"><span><i></i> Primary / foreign key indicators</span><span>1 user → multiple motorcycles</span><span>Bookings connect users, workshops and services</span></div>
  <p class="erd-disclaimer">Illustrative entity relationship diagram for product communication. Table names, fields, cardinalities and key constraints should be updated to match the actual schema. For production documentation, include order items, payment records, reviews, notifications and audit fields only where they are genuinely implemented.</p>
  <div class="visual-stack" style="margin-top:30px">
   <figure class="visual-card reveal">
