 <div class="container">
  <div class="section-head reveal"><div><div class="eyebrow">05 / Core engineering concepts</div><h2>The craft behind<br><em>the interface.</em></h2></div><p>A professional mobile experience depends on more than attractive screens. These are the engineering ideas worth communicating to a potential client.</p></div>
  <div class="concept-grid">
   <article class="concept-card reveal"><div class="concept-top"><span class="concept-icon">▦</span><span>CORE 01</span></div><h3>Reusable UI system</h3><p>Consistent service cards, buttons, status labels, form fields and spacing reduce visual drift and make future screens faster to build.</p></article>
   <article class="concept-card reveal delay-1"><div class="concept-top"><span class="concept-icon">⌘</span><span>CORE 02</span></div><h3>Predictable state</h3><p>Represent loading, success, validation and failure states clearly so users understand the result of an action and what to do next.</p></article>
   <article class="concept-card reveal delay-2"><div class="concept-top"><span class="concept-icon">⇄</span><span>CORE 03</span></div><h3>Separated responsibilities</h3><p>Keep presentation, application rules and data access distinct where appropriate, improving maintainability and testability.</p></article>
   <article class="concept-card reveal"><div class="concept-top"><span class="concept-icon">✓</span><span>CORE 04</span></div><h3>Input validation</h3><p>Validate booking details and required fields early, with helpful feedback instead of silent failures or confusing form behavior.</p></article>
   <article class="concept-card reveal delay-1"><div class="concept-top"><span class="concept-icon">◷</span><span>CORE 05</span></div><h3>Time-slot integrity</h3><p>Appointment flows need clear availability, timezone-aware dates and server-side checks to avoid conflicting reservations.</p></article>
   <article class="concept-card reveal delay-2"><div class="concept-top"><span class="concept-icon">⌁</span><span>CORE 06</span></div><h3>Reliable data handling</h3><p>Model relationships carefully, handle network errors and protect account data through appropriate authentication and authorization.</p></article>
